an style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> {</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">    #[error(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"amount must be positive, got {0:?}\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">    NonPositiveAmount</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Paise</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">),</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">    #[error(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"amount overflowed the ledger's range\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">    Overflow</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">,</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">    #[error(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"account {0} is frozen\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">    AccountFrozen</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">AccountId</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">),</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">    #[error(</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#96D0FF\">\"insufficient funds: needed {needed:?}, available {available:?}\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">    InsufficientFunds</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> { needed</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> Paise</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">, available</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\"> Paise</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\"> },</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">    #[error(transparent)]</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#DCBDFB\">    Db</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">(#[from] </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">sqlx</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F47067\">::</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#F69D50\">Error</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">),</span></span>\n<span data-line=\"\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#ADBAC7\">}</span></span></code></pre></figure>\n<p>Each variant carries the numbers involved. When support asks \"why was this\nrejected\", the answer is in the log line, not in a reconstruction.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-to-steal-for-your-own-project\">What to steal for your own project</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Newtypes for every unit.</strong> <code>Paise</code>, <code>Bps</code>, <code>AccountId</code>, <code>IdempotencyKey</code>. The\ncompiler then prevents the class of bug where two <code>i64</code>s get swapped.</li>\n<li><strong><code>checked_*</code> everywhere money is involved.</strong> Set\n<code>[lints.clippy] arithmetic_side_effects = \"deny\"</code> in the crate that owns the\nledger.</li>\n<li><strong>Append-only tables.</strong> <code>UPDATE balance</code> is how you lose an audit trail.</li>\n<li><strong>Reconciliation as a test, not a runbook.</strong> A proptest that generates random\ntransfers and asserts <code>sum(entries) == 0</code> per transfer catches most real bugs.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"where-rust-is-the-wrong-answer\">Where Rust is the wrong answer</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Back-office reporting and ad-hoc queries: use SQL, in the database.</li>\n<li>Pricing experiments and analytics: the tooling is Python's, and that is fine.</li>\n<li>Anything with a hard regulatory deadline and no Rust team: the migration risk\noutweighs the correctness gain.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"try-it\">Try it</h2>\n<p>Write the <code>Transfer</code> type above, then write a proptest that generates 10,000 random\ntransfers between 100 accounts and asserts two invariants: every transfer nets to\nzero, and <code>sum(all ledger deltas) == 0</code>. If both hold after a random kill -9 in the\nmiddle, your ledger is sound.</p>\n<p><strong>Next:</strong> <a href=\"05-embedded-and-safety.md\">Embedded and safety-critical</a></p>"}